From: Nura <nura@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/mediatek: attach mmap offset for dumb buffers up front

The vendor mtk-drm GEM object funcs only provide ->free, ->get_sg_table and
->vm_ops, but no ->mmap. The PRIME mmap path (drm_gem_prime_mmap) therefore
falls back to drm_gem_mmap(), which looks the object up by its fake vma
offset. That offset is only created when userspace issues
DRM_IOCTL_MODE_MAP_DUMB.

KWin with a software renderer (llvmpipe) imports the dumb buffers as
dma-bufs and mmaps them directly, so the import fails with -EINVAL and the
screen stays black. Create the fake offset in dumb_create so any PRIME
consumer can mmap the buffer.

---
 drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_drm_gem.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_drm_gem.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_drm_gem.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_drm_gem.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_drm_gem.c
@@ -387,6 +387,19 @@ int mtk_drm_gem_dumb_create(struct drm_file *file_priv, struct drm_device *dev,
 	if (IS_ERR(mtk_gem))
 		return PTR_ERR(mtk_gem);
 
+	/*
+	 * Nura: attach the fake mmap offset up front. The PRIME mmap path
+	 * (drm_gem_prime_mmap) falls back to drm_gem_mmap() when the object
+	 * has no ->mmap callback, and that lookup requires this offset. KWin
+	 * with the software renderer (llvmpipe) imports these dumb buffers as
+	 * dma-bufs and mmaps them directly, without ever issuing
+	 * DRM_IOCTL_MODE_MAP_DUMB, so the import failed with -EINVAL and the
+	 * screen stayed black.
+	 */
+	ret = drm_gem_create_mmap_offset(&mtk_gem->base);
+	if (ret)
+		goto err_handle_create;
+
 	/*
 	 * allocate a id of idr table where the obj is registered
 	 * and handle has the id what user can see.
